":"0 ..< P_s"},{"type":"text","text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_s + q"},{"type":"text","text":" is target incidence "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, and of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inHyperedgeIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not offer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs":{"title":"Hypergraphs","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods. In-adjacency usually costs extra"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage, so representations that store only out-adjacency conform to "},